  "interpretation": {
    "publication_method": "For the single BMP producer, subtract queue publication delta from latest-sample attempt sequence delta between successful endpoint publications. This counts unpublished attempts inside those endpoints, not attempts outside the boundaries. Runtime, profile, timestamps and counters were checked for resets/changes.",
    "before": "120 seconds: 50 unpublished BMP attempts, 21 stale snapshots, 8 new global missed-heartbeat events.",
    "after": "600 seconds: 1200 BMP attempt-sequence increments and 1200 publications; all 4380 BMP and radar snapshots fresh; zero new timeout, framing, I/O, UART-overrun or missed-heartbeat events.",
    "causal_scope": "Code and forced-preemption fixture establish the contention mechanism. Before/after observation supports this fix for the BMP publication gaps. Global counters do not identify which worker missed a heartbeat. No claim that the original intermittent UART failure is solved.",
    "queue_overwrites": "Event 4 rose by 13281 after the fix. These are bounded application FIFO drop_oldest overwrites, not UART receive overruns. OLED reads latest-sample cache and does not consume FIFO entries.",
    "sampling_limits": "Requested 137 ms read-only snapshots are observations, not execution traces or independent sensor samples. Events/stale periods between observations can be missed. Counters may undercount if contention exhausts retries.",
    "oled": "User confirmed readable and updating after final application installation; visible latency not instrumented.",
    "radar_absence": "User explicitly deferred further zero-target checks. Uncontrolled target counts are not absence acceptance or training labels.",
    "ai": "No training or deployment. Preserve original study/model/frozen sources. New build identity, frozen study/evaluation groups and fresh repetitions are required for further training."
  },
